.TH PSMatrixCopy 3 2023-12-03 "PsyC 0.9.3" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
PSMatrixCopy

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/maths.h>

.I
int  
.br
\fBPSMatrixCopy\fR(\fIPSMatrix src\fR, \fIPSMatrix dst\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copy values of matrix \fIsrc\fR to matrix \fIdst\fR. Both \fIsrc\fR and \fIdst\fR must have the same shape.
.br

.br
\fBNOTE\fR:  if \fIdst\fR owns a cached transposed version of itself, the cached version will be cleared. At the same time, if \fIdst\fR is the cached transposed version of another matrix, the cached version of the owner matrix will be cleared.
.br

.SH RETURN VALUES
1 in case of success, 0 if:

.RS 4
\[bu] \fIsrc\fR is \fINULL\fR or \fIdst\fR is \fINULL\fR.
.br

\[bu] \fIsrc\fR and \fIdst\fR have different shapes.
.br
.RE
